# Security Configuration for Karate Scoring System

## Security Measures Implemented:

### 1. Electron Security
- ✅ Disabled nodeIntegration in renderer processes
- ✅ Enabled contextIsolation for all windows
- ✅ Implemented secure preload script for IPC communication
- ✅ Whitelisted IPC channels for security

### 2. Input Sanitization
- ✅ Added input sanitization for all user inputs
- ✅ HTML tag removal and special character encoding
- ✅ XSS prevention in notifications and display components

### 3. Error Handling
- ✅ Added null checks for DOM elements
- ✅ Wrapped IPC listeners in try-catch blocks
- ✅ Validation for score data properties

### 4. Code Quality
- ✅ Removed unsafe innerHTML usage where possible
- ✅ Implemented safe DOM manipulation methods
- ✅ Added input validation for all forms

### 5. Performance Improvements
- ✅ Cached DOM element references where appropriate
- ✅ Optimized repeated DOM queries
- ✅ Improved timer display efficiency

## Remaining Recommendations:

1. Consider implementing user authentication for web judges
2. Add HTTPS support for web judge server in production
3. Implement rate limiting for web judge connections
4. Add logging and monitoring for security events
5. Regular security audits and dependency updates

## Usage Notes:

- All renderer processes now use secure IPC communication
- User inputs are automatically sanitized
- Error handling prevents application crashes
- Performance optimizations reduce resource usage